values ('a7c8d9e0-1f2a-4b77-8c67-7d8e9f0a1b27', 'learning-and-behavior', 'Learning and Behavior', 'Define learning as behavior change through experience, connect major traditions, and establish the course''s experimental and applied logic. Topics explain classical and operant conditioning, reinforcement, punishment, avoidance, schedules, choice, extinction, relapse, and stimulus control; observational learning; cognitive, neural, and evolutionary perspectives; motivation, emotion, stress, skill learning, habits, and self-regulation; behavior modification and applied behavior analysis; learning in education, health, organizations, and technology; and contemporary debates, computational models, and a capstone behavior-change project.');

